	<item>
		<title>Using the Import &#038; Export Feature in FeedOps for Bulk Product Updates</title>
		<link>https://feedops.com/demo/import-export-bulk-product-data/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jazib Zaidi]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 04 Mar 2025 22:43:19 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">https://feedops.com/?post_type=demo&#038;p=4533</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>This video provides a step-by-step guide on how to use the Import &#38; Export feature in FeedOps to efficiently update product attributes, such as GTIN, in bulk. Keeping product data accurate is essential for optimizing feed performance, and this feature streamlines the process by allowing bulk edits via spreadsheet imports. Step-by-Step Guide: Exporting Your Product [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/import-export-bulk-product-data/">Using the Import &amp; Export Feature in FeedOps for Bulk Product Updates</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[		<div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="4533" class="elementor elementor-4533" data-elementor-post-type="demo">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-3ba9ba71 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="3ba9ba71" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2fe67b89 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="2fe67b89" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									
<p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">This video provides a step-by-step guide on how to use the Import &amp; Export feature in FeedOps to efficiently update product attributes, such as GTIN, in bulk. Keeping product data accurate is essential for optimizing feed performance, and this feature streamlines the process by allowing bulk edits via spreadsheet imports.</p>
<p><strong>Step-by-Step Guide:</strong></p>
<ol start="1" data-spread="true">
<li>
<p><strong>Exporting Your Product Feed:</strong></p>
<ul data-spread="false">
<li>
<p>Navigate to the Products screen in FeedOps.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Click the Column button to search and select the attribute you want to update (e.g., GTIN).</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Use the Filter option to find products missing the attribute (e.g., set GTIN is empty).</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Click the Export button to download a spreadsheet with the selected products.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Open the exported file in Excel, Google Sheets, or another spreadsheet tool and update the missing values.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Importing the Updated File:</strong></p>
<ul data-spread="false">
<li>
<p>Return to FeedOps and click Import from the table action menu.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Select the source file format (CSV, TSV, XML, or compressed versions like ZIP, GZIP, BZIP2).</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>If using Google Sheets, sign in and grant access to FeedOps, then select the updated sheet.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Mapping Product Attributes:</strong></p>
<ul data-spread="false">
<li>
<p>Ensure the correct mapping of attributes such as GTIN, Brand, and Title.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>If importing a file originally exported from FeedOps, the mapping will be automatic.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Verify that Product ID matches correctly to prevent duplicate entries.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Finalizing the Import:</strong></p>
<ul data-spread="false">
<li>
<p>Review the mapped attributes and click Save to start the import process.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>FeedOps will apply updates and refresh the product feed with the latest data.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Key Takeaways:</strong></p>
<ul data-spread="false">
<li>
<p>Use the Import &amp; Export feature to update product attributes in bulk efficiently.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Filtering helps target specific products missing key data.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Ensure correct attribute mapping to avoid errors during import.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Compatible with multiple file formats, including Google Sheets integration.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Contents:</strong></p>
<ul data-spread="false">
<li>
<p>Introduction to Import &amp; Export Feature</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Why Bulk Updates Are Important</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Exporting Product Data</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Editing Data in a Spreadsheet</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Importing Updated Files into FeedOps</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Mapping and Finalizing the Import</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Summary and Benefits</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>This guide ensures that your product feed remains accurate and up to date, enhancing performance with minimal manual effort.</p>
								</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/import-export-bulk-product-data/">Using the Import &amp; Export Feature in FeedOps for Bulk Product Updates</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Using Feed Rules to Automate Feed Optimization</title>
		<link>https://feedops.com/demo/using-feed-rules-to-automate-optimization/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jazib Zaidi]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 26 Feb 2025 03:56:39 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">https://feedops.com/?post_type=demo&#038;p=4528</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>This demo provides a step-by-step walkthrough of the Feed Rules feature in FeedOps, which allows users to define conditions that automatically adjust product attributes. This helps streamline feed management by ensuring accurate, up-to-date data across different sales channels. Overview of the Video: Introduction to Feed Rules and their benefits Navigating to the Feed Rules screen [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/using-feed-rules-to-automate-optimization/">Using Feed Rules to Automate Feed Optimization</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[		<div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="4528" class="elementor elementor-4528" data-elementor-post-type="demo">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-ef9a466 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="ef9a466" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-d9337a0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="d9337a0" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p data-start="1579" data-end="1893">This demo provides a step-by-step walkthrough of the <strong data-start="1662" data-end="1676">Feed Rules</strong> feature in FeedOps, which allows users to define conditions that automatically adjust product attributes. This helps streamline feed management by ensuring accurate, up-to-date data across different sales channels.</p><h3 data-start="1895" data-end="1927"><strong data-start="1899" data-end="1925">Overview of the Video:</strong></h3><ul data-start="1928" data-end="2213"><li data-start="1928" data-end="1977">Introduction to Feed Rules and their benefits</li><li data-start="1978" data-end="2028">Navigating to the Feed Rules screen in FeedOps</li><li data-start="2029" data-end="2113">Creating a rule to assign a missing product color based on keywords in the title</li><li data-start="2114" data-end="2157">Setting conditions and defining actions</li><li data-start="2158" data-end="2213">Previewing and applying the rule to ensure accuracy</li></ul><h3 data-start="2215" data-end="2239"><strong data-start="2219" data-end="2237">Key Takeaways:</strong></h3><ul data-start="2240" data-end="2527"><li data-start="2240" data-end="2323">Feed Rules help automate product attribute adjustments based on set conditions.</li><li data-start="2324" data-end="2397">Users can create rules to transform, clean, or enhance product feeds.</li><li data-start="2398" data-end="2463">The Preview feature ensures accuracy before applying changes.</li><li data-start="2464" data-end="2527">Rules can be customized to override manual edits if needed.</li></ul><p data-start="2529" data-end="2544"><strong data-start="2529" data-end="2542">Contents:</strong></p><ul data-start="2545" data-end="2687"><li data-start="2545" data-end="2561">Introduction</li><li data-start="2562" data-end="2590">Navigating to Feed Rules</li><li data-start="2591" data-end="2614">Creating a new rule</li><li data-start="2615" data-end="2651">Assigning attributes dynamically</li><li data-start="2652" data-end="2687">Previewing and applying updates</li></ul>								</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/using-feed-rules-to-automate-optimization/">Using Feed Rules to Automate Feed Optimization</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Use the Feed Editor to Update Product Attributes</title>
		<link>https://feedops.com/demo/use-the-feed-editor-to-update-product-attributes/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jazib Zaidi]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 14 Feb 2025 03:59:04 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">https://feedops.com/?post_type=demo&#038;p=4521</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Learn how to efficiently update product attributes using the Feed Editor in FeedOps. Customize Your View: Select only the columns you need, such as Material, Brand, or Color. Filter Products: Apply filters to update specific items, like products with &#8220;Leather&#8221; in the title. Edit in Bulk: Make changes across multiple products at once for consistency. [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/use-the-feed-editor-to-update-product-attributes/">Use the Feed Editor to Update Product Attributes</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[		<div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="4521" class="elementor elementor-4521" data-elementor-post-type="demo">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-fcc34cd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="fcc34cd" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-cbe1ba7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="cbe1ba7" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p data-start="81" data-end="190">Learn how to efficiently update product attributes using the <strong data-start="161" data-end="176">Feed Editor</strong> in FeedOps.</p><ul data-start="192" data-end="581"><li data-start="192" data-end="289"><strong data-start="194" data-end="217">Customize Your View</strong>: Select only the columns you need, such as Material, Brand, or Color.</li><li data-start="290" data-end="397"><strong data-start="292" data-end="311">Filter Products</strong>: Apply filters to update specific items, like products with &#8220;Leather&#8221; in the title.</li><li data-start="398" data-end="482"><strong data-start="400" data-end="416">Edit in Bulk</strong>: Make changes across multiple products at once for consistency.</li><li data-start="483" data-end="581"><strong data-start="485" data-end="505">Automate Updates</strong>: Use Feed Rules to dynamically adjust attributes based on set conditions.</li></ul><p data-start="583" data-end="649" data-is-last-node="">Keep your product feed accurate and optimized with minimal effort.</p>								</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/use-the-feed-editor-to-update-product-attributes/">Use the Feed Editor to Update Product Attributes</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Manage Product Listings with Custom Labels in FeedOps</title>
		<link>https://feedops.com/demo/manage-product-listings-with-custom-labels-in-feedops/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jazib Zaidi]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 14 Feb 2025 03:42:55 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">https://feedops.com/?post_type=demo&#038;p=4520</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In this tutorial, we guide you through the process of using custom labels in FeedOps to improve product segmentation and optimize ad performance across platforms like Google Shopping, Microsoft Ads, and Meta. By categorizing products with custom labels, you can create highly targeted campaigns, ensuring better budget allocation and improved ROAS. Key Steps Covered: Accessing [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/manage-product-listings-with-custom-labels-in-feedops/">Manage Product Listings with Custom Labels in FeedOps</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[		<div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="4520" class="elementor elementor-4520" data-elementor-post-type="demo">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-ca38be1 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="ca38be1" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-176390e elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="176390e" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p data-start="67" data-end="429">In this tutorial, we guide you through the process of using <strong data-start="127" data-end="144">custom labels</strong> in FeedOps to improve product segmentation and optimize ad performance across platforms like <strong data-start="238" data-end="282">Google Shopping, Microsoft Ads, and Meta</strong>. By categorizing products with custom labels, you can create <strong data-start="344" data-end="373">highly targeted campaigns</strong>, ensuring better budget allocation and improved ROAS.</p><h3 data-start="431" data-end="459"><strong data-start="435" data-end="457">Key Steps Covered:</strong></h3><ul data-start="461" data-end="1381"><li data-start="461" data-end="591"><p data-start="463" data-end="591"><strong data-start="463" data-end="491">Accessing Custom Labels:</strong> Navigate to the <strong data-start="508" data-end="526">&#8216;Product Feed&#8217;</strong> section in FeedOps and locate the <strong data-start="561" data-end="580">&#8216;Custom Labels&#8217;</strong> feature.</p></li><li data-start="593" data-end="766"><p data-start="595" data-end="766"><strong data-start="595" data-end="636">Applying Labels with the Bulk Editor:</strong> Use the bulk editor to quickly assign labels to selected products based on existing attributes like title, category, or margin.</p></li><li data-start="768" data-end="962"><p data-start="770" data-end="962"><strong data-start="770" data-end="808">Automating Labels with Feed Rules:</strong> Set up Feed Rules to dynamically apply custom labels when new products meet specific conditions (e.g., product title contains &#8220;Summer&#8221; or &#8220;Clearance&#8221;).</p></li><li data-start="964" data-end="1172"><p data-start="966" data-end="1172"><strong data-start="966" data-end="1009">Using Metafields for Advanced Labeling:</strong> Leverage metafields in your eCommerce platform to assign labels to products that are not easily filtered through standard attributes (e.g., drop-shipped items).</p></li><li data-start="1174" data-end="1381"><p data-start="1176" data-end="1381"><strong data-start="1176" data-end="1210">Reviewing and Syncing Updates:</strong> Once custom labels are applied, review them and sync your feed to ensure the changes reflect in your <strong data-start="1312" data-end="1378">Google Merchant Center, Microsoft Advertising, or Meta catalog</strong>.</p></li></ul><h3 data-start="1383" data-end="1419"><strong data-start="1387" data-end="1417">Benefits of Custom Labels:</strong></h3><p data-start="1421" data-end="1864">Implementing custom labels allows advertisers to:<br data-start="1470" data-end="1473" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/2705.png" alt="✅" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <strong data-start="1475" data-end="1505">Improve campaign targeting</strong> by grouping products based on seasonality, margins, or inventory type.<br data-start="1576" data-end="1579" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/2705.png" alt="✅" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <strong data-start="1581" data-end="1610">Enhance budget efficiency</strong> by prioritizing high-margin or best-selling products.<br data-start="1664" data-end="1667" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/2705.png" alt="✅" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <strong data-start="1669" data-end="1699">Streamline feed management</strong> with automated rules that update labels as new products are added.<br data-start="1766" data-end="1769" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/2705.png" alt="✅" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <strong data-start="1771" data-end="1788">Maximize ROAS</strong> by segmenting and bidding more effectively across different ad platforms.</p><p data-start="1866" data-end="2061" data-is-last-node="">By leveraging <strong data-start="1880" data-end="1921">FeedOps&#8217; Custom Labels and Feed Rules</strong>, eCommerce businesses can take full control of their product feed strategy, ensuring better ad placement and improved campaign performance.</p>								</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/manage-product-listings-with-custom-labels-in-feedops/">Manage Product Listings with Custom Labels in FeedOps</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Creating Google Promotion IDs in FeedOps</title>
		<link>https://feedops.com/demo/creating-google-promotion-ids-in-feedops/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jazib Zaidi]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 30 Jan 2025 21:07:51 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">https://feedops.com/?post_type=platform-demo&#038;p=4338</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Overview This guide explains how Promotion IDs work within Google Merchant Center to track and manage specific promotions, such as free shipping or buy-one-get-one-free (BOGO) deals, directly linked to your ads. Learn when to use these identifiers to maximize ad performance and ensure promotions are applicable at checkout, complying fully with Google&#8217;s advertising policies. Discover [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/creating-google-promotion-ids-in-feedops/">Creating Google Promotion IDs in FeedOps</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[		<div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="4338" class="elementor elementor-4338" data-elementor-post-type="demo">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-f2bfa58 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="f2bfa58" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-dcfe4cb elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="dcfe4cb" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<span class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Overview</span>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2243ee7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="2243ee7" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>This guide explains how Promotion IDs work within Google Merchant Center to track and manage specific promotions, such as free shipping or buy-one-get-one-free (BOGO) deals, directly linked to your ads. Learn when to use these identifiers to maximize ad performance and ensure promotions are applicable at checkout, complying fully with Google&#8217;s advertising policies. Discover how to create and manage Promotion IDs using FeedOps, simplifying the process of syncing promotions with your Merchant Center to improve conversion rates effectively.</p><h3><strong>Examples of Effective Promotions Using IDs:</strong></h3><ul><li><strong>Free Shipping:</strong> Connect free shipping offers on select products or orders above a certain value directly to your ads.</li><li><strong>BOGO Deals:</strong> Apply buy-one-get-one-free promotions to specific items or categories, ensuring conditions like minimum purchases are met.</li></ul><h3><strong>Setting Up Promotion IDs in FeedOps:</strong></h3><ol><li>Navigate to the product screen.</li><li>Filter by attributes such as brand or product category.</li><li>Add a Promotion ID column and input your ID (e.g., BOGO-2025) for targeted products.</li><li>Publish the rule to sync with Merchant Center.</li></ol><h3><strong>Using Feed Rules for Dynamic Promotions:</strong></h3><ul><li>Set up Promotion IDs with feed rules for items with high inventory turnover, such as &#8220;sports socks,&#8221; to ensure the promotion adjusts automatically with inventory changes.</li></ul><h3><strong>Finalizing Promotions in Google Merchant Center:</strong></h3><ul><li>Create your promotion using the established Promotion ID in FeedOps to ensure your shopping ads are accurately labeled, enhancing click-through and conversion rates.</li><li>Leverage this feature to ensure that your promotional offers are not only attractive but also perfectly aligned with the shopper&#8217;s expectations, driving more sales through your Google Shopping campaigns.</li></ul>								</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/creating-google-promotion-ids-in-feedops/">Creating Google Promotion IDs in FeedOps</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Edit Product Types Using the Bulk Editor in FeedOps</title>
		<link>https://feedops.com/demo/edit-product-types-using-the-bulk-editor/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jazib Zaidi]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 30 Jan 2025 21:05:47 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">https://feedops.com/?post_type=platform-demo&#038;p=4337</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Overview In this comprehensive tutorial, we guide you through manually adding product types to your feed using FeedOps&#8217; Bulk Editor. This process enhances product categorization, leading to improved feed optimization across platforms like Google Shopping, Microsoft Ads, and other prominent eCommerce channels. Key Takeaways: Navigating the FeedOps Interface: Access the &#8216;Products&#8217; tab and select your [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/edit-product-types-using-the-bulk-editor/">Edit Product Types Using the Bulk Editor in FeedOps</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[		<div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="4337" class="elementor elementor-4337" data-elementor-post-type="demo">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-76a5272 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="76a5272" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-ed6130c elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="ed6130c" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Overview</h3>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-f91685a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="f91685a" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>In this comprehensive tutorial, we guide you through manually adding product types to your feed using FeedOps&#8217; Bulk Editor. This process enhances product categorization, leading to improved feed optimization across platforms like Google Shopping, Microsoft Ads, and other prominent eCommerce channels.</p><p><strong>Key Takeaways:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Navigating the FeedOps Interface:</strong> Access the &#8216;Products&#8217; tab and select your desired channel (e.g., Google Shopping, Microsoft Ads).</p></li><li><p><strong>Filtering Products:</strong> Utilize filters to identify specific products, such as those with certain keywords in their titles.</p></li><li><p><strong>Assigning Product Types:</strong> Add detailed product type categorizations to organize your products better and enhance their visibility.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Step-by-Step Process:</strong></p><ol><li><p><strong>Access the Products Tab:</strong> Navigate to the &#8216;Products&#8217; section in FeedOps and choose your target channel.</p></li><li><p><strong>Customize Columns:</strong> Add relevant columns for categorization, including Product Type Levels 1–5.</p></li><li><p><strong>Apply Filters:</strong> Filter your product list using conditions like title keywords to narrow down the selection.</p></li><li><p><strong>Select and Edit Products:</strong> Choose the products you wish to edit, update their product types accordingly, and save the changes.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Practical Example:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Product Type Level 3:</strong> Assign &#8220;Wool Socks.&#8221;</p></li><li><p><strong>Product Type Level 4:</strong> Assign &#8220;Australian-Made Socks.&#8221;</p></li><li><p><strong>Product Type Level 5:</strong> Assign &#8220;Non-Elastic Top Socks.&#8221;</p></li></ul><p><strong>Importance of Detailed Categorization:</strong></p><p>Organizing your products with specific product type levels ensures accurate representation on advertising platforms like Google Shopping and Microsoft Ads. This precision enhances product visibility, relevance, and overall campaign performance.</p><p>For a visual demonstration, you can watch the following tutorial:</p>								</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/edit-product-types-using-the-bulk-editor/">Edit Product Types Using the Bulk Editor in FeedOps</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Enhance Product Categorization with FeedOps AI</title>
		<link>https://feedops.com/demo/enhance-product-categorization-with-feedops-ai/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jazib Zaidi]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 30 Jan 2025 20:35:05 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">https://feedops.com/?post_type=help_video&#038;p=4328</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Overview In this comprehensive tutorial, we demonstrate how FeedOps&#8217; AI streamlines the correction of missing product types in your shopping feeds. By leveraging powerful AI tools, you can effortlessly optimize your product data. The video covers several key aspects: Accessing the &#8220;Missing Product Types Detected&#8221; Card: Learn to navigate to this feature within the FeedOps [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/enhance-product-categorization-with-feedops-ai/">Enhance Product Categorization with FeedOps AI</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[		<div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="4328" class="elementor elementor-4328" data-elementor-post-type="demo">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-69bb113 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="69bb113" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-66b5772 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="66b5772" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Overview</h3>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-c655a18 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="c655a18" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>In this comprehensive tutorial, we demonstrate how FeedOps&#8217; AI streamlines the correction of missing product types in your shopping feeds. By leveraging powerful AI tools, you can effortlessly optimize your product data. The video covers several key aspects:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Accessing the &#8220;Missing Product Types Detected&#8221; Card:</strong> Learn to navigate to this feature within the FeedOps Playbook to identify products lacking proper categorization.</p></li><li><p><strong>Selecting Products and Managing AI Credits:</strong> Understand how to choose products with missing types and efficiently allocate AI credits for processing.</p></li><li><p><strong>Utilizing AI for Tailored Product Type Suggestions:</strong> Discover how FeedOps&#8217; AI analyzes your product data to recommend appropriate categories that suit your specific needs.</p></li><li><p><strong>Reviewing and Applying AI-Generated Recommendations:</strong> Follow the steps to assess AI suggestions and implement them to enhance your product feed&#8217;s structure.</p></li><li><p><strong>Monitoring Updates and Tracking AI Credits:</strong> Keep track of the changes made, manage your AI credit usage, and review completed optimizations to ensure continuous improvement.</p></li></ul><p>By adopting FeedOps&#8217; AI capabilities, you can significantly reduce manual efforts, ensuring your product feed is accurate and well-structured. This leads to improved performance in advertising campaigns across platforms like Google Shopping and Microsoft Ads. Begin optimizing your product data today with FeedOps AI to gain better control and achieve superior results.</p>								</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/enhance-product-categorization-with-feedops-ai/">Enhance Product Categorization with FeedOps AI</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Automate Product Types with Feed Rules in FeedOps</title>
		<link>https://feedops.com/demo/automate-product-types-with-feed-rules/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jazib Zaidi]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 30 Jan 2025 18:14:31 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">https://feedops.com/?post_type=help_video&#038;p=4318</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Overview In this comprehensive tutorial, we guide you through the process of automating product type assignments using FeedOps&#8217; Feed Rules feature. By setting specific conditions and applying custom attributes, you can efficiently categorize your products, enhancing feed optimization for platforms like Google Shopping, Microsoft Ads, and other prominent eCommerce channels. Key Steps Covered: Accessing Feed [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/automate-product-types-with-feed-rules/">Automate Product Types with Feed Rules in FeedOps</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[		<div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="4318" class="elementor elementor-4318" data-elementor-post-type="demo">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-44ebeae e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="44ebeae" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-68ae548 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="68ae548" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Overview</h3>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-57e6836 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="57e6836" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>In this comprehensive tutorial, we guide you through the process of automating product type assignments using FeedOps&#8217; Feed Rules feature. By setting specific conditions and applying custom attributes, you can efficiently categorize your products, enhancing feed optimization for platforms like Google Shopping, Microsoft Ads, and other prominent eCommerce channels.</p><p><strong>Key Steps Covered:</strong></p><ol><li><p><strong>Accessing Feed Rules:</strong> Navigate to the &#8216;Website Settings&#8217; in FeedOps and select &#8216;Feed Rules&#8217; to begin the setup process.</p></li><li><p><strong>Creating a New Rule:</strong> Add a new rule, naming it appropriately (e.g., &#8220;Product Type 4 &amp; 5 Assignment&#8221;), and select the channels to which it will apply.</p></li><li><p><strong>Defining Conditions:</strong> Set conditions to group products based on specific criteria, such as product titles containing the word &#8216;Wool&#8217;.</p></li><li><p><strong>Assigning Actions:</strong> Specify the desired product type levels (e.g., Levels 4 and 5) and input the corresponding custom attributes to categorize the selected products accurately.</p></li><li><p><strong>Saving and Activating the Rule:</strong> After configuring the conditions and actions, save the rule as a draft, review it for accuracy, and then apply it to activate the automated categorization.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Benefits of Automation:</strong></p><p>Implementing automated product type assignments streamlines your feed management process, reducing the need for manual edits. This approach ensures consistent and accurate product categorization, leading to improved visibility and performance in advertising campaigns across various platforms.</p><p>By leveraging FeedOps&#8217; Feed Rules, eCommerce businesses can enhance their advertising efficiency, ensuring products are appropriately categorized and displayed to potential customers.</p>								</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/demo/automate-product-types-with-feed-rules/">Automate Product Types with Feed Rules in FeedOps</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
	</channel>
